From f5cc59001c2e5d297e3a4c592bd6797ea8feecf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen38-4090 <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:34:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] research38d: NINFER_ATTN_FILL_FIT=1 sizes the
 row-split/row-pair L2 fill to the spare resident slots (off)

One fill slice whose first fill_ctas CTAs (the slots two CTAs per SM leave next to the attention CTAs) each keep 16
lines per thread in flight; the rest of the slice exits. Bit-exact (fills only prefetch; ids 482/482). nsys: the
row-pair kernel gets slower (12.35 -> 14.40 us; 16 SMs cannot pull 8 MB as fast as 48 CTAs), GEMMs unchanged; the
forced A B A B is within run-to-run variation (-0.19% under a linear drift + cold-first-run model). Default off.
---
 .../dense/causal_cache/small_t_k8v4.cu        | 35 ++++++++++++--
 .../causal_cache/small_t_k8v4_rowsplit.cuh    | 46 +++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ops/softmax_attention/dense/causal_cache/small_t_k8v4.cu b/src/ops/softmax_attention/dense/causal_cache/small_t_k8v4.cu
